characters.appearance:
Wang Xi is consistently depicted as a woman of breathtaking beauty, described as "beautiful... not nearly real" (美丽的近乎不真实), emphasizing an almost otherworldly or celestial quality to her allure. Her physique is noted as "tall and graceful" (身姿高挑而婀娜), with a "dim curve" that even a long skirt cannot fully conceal, suggesting a captivating and elegant figure. She possesses an oval face (瓜子脸) that shines "white like semi-transparent jade" (莹白如羊脂玉), a common metaphor signifying purity, preciousness, and a flawless complexion. Her eyebrows are dark and curved (黛眉弯弯), her eyes are likened to "black gems" (眸若黑宝石), and she has a finely sculpted, upturned nose described as a "fine jade nose" (琼鼻挺翘). Complementing these features are her red lips (红唇点点) and "pearly white sparkling and translucent" teeth (贝齿晶莹).

Wang Xi's hair is a prominent feature, described as a "full head [of] beautiful hair [that] dances in the air" (满头秀发飞舞) during combat , or as smooth and lustrous, like "silk fabrics" (一头秀发光滑若绸缎). Her overall presence exudes a luminous quality, with her skin having a "luster Yingying" (肌肤光泽莹莹), and her gait is so graceful it is likened to a "divine lotus drags" , suggesting an ethereal and dignified movement. &#160;

Her smile is particularly noteworthy for its profound impact. Though sometimes "very light," it is described as "very shocking, such as an immortal flower blooms, suddenly made the entire whole world bright". Even when her smile is not overtly warm or might appear "a little pale," it possesses the power to cause a cultivator's heart to "tense play jump". This powerful effect of her smile, even when subdued, indicates a charisma that transcends simple emotional expression, hinting at an innate magnetism or a profound inner spirit that captivates those around her. The consistent use of terms like jade, gems, and radiance in her descriptions reinforces her image as a "Fairy Maiden" (仙子), a title also used for her in the context of her having cultivated three strands of Immortal Qi.
